A||N||6||tesmith66||Console Restoration - Which Glue??||||5||
Z||000000||tesmith66||11-16-2001||12:09 PM||||I'm ready to restore my console (basically glue and clamp all of the curled edges down). I saw an article on the net about this, but can't find the glue the author specified.<P>Has anyone else done this?? What glue did you use? I live in the St. Louis area, so I need something that can withstand high heat and humidity as well as bitter cold.<P>Thanks in advance for your help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-16-2001||12:45 PM||||I used super glue and the spray accelerator that makes it stick NOW.  You don't need to clamp, just do about an inch at a time and you can hold it for 10 sec with your fingers after spraying the accellerator on.  It dries very quick and is very strong.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||11-16-2001||12:49 PM||||Ditto.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-16-2001||01:31 PM||||Guess I'm old fashioned.  I used two-part epoxy and clamped evertything up overnite.  Not as quick, but hopefully just as effective.||||reg||10
Z||000004||tesmith66||11-16-2001||02:03 PM||||Can I get the super glue and accelerant at Home Depot or Lowe's, or do I go to a craft store like Frank's or Michael's??<P><P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||5
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-16-2001||04:29 PM||||Gorilla Glue.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||11-16-2001||04:48 PM||||I used 3M Trim Adhesive. It's what the pros use to reattach loose trim on cars. You can only get it at an automotive paint supply store It's not cheap ($18 per bottle) but I can tell you, it worked like nothing else. I got this advise from DXR_DAD. Use just a little and clamp it for a couple of seconds and it's done. It's been over a year since I've repaired mine. I live in Tampa, Florida and drive the car everyday rain, heat, cold, snow (Oh, wait, we don't have snow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) and there is no hint of it letting loose. I actually think it slightly melted the plastic and vinyl and welded them together. Great stuff!<P>------------------<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
